t(38, 845, """Every wronged person will certainly be given victory .. When people are wronged they say: "When?" Indeed, injustice is a test for the wrongdoer, and "when" is a test for the wronged! The prayer of the wronged — by Allah, by Allah, by Allah — is answered, if Allah wills, if Allah intends and if Allah permits .. It is among the most shaking and loudest of prayers, because it is proof of a challenge to Allah the Almighty that took place on earth .. For when our Almighty Lord, hallowed be His names, tells us "Do not wrong one another" and we do wrong, that is a challenge to Allah Most High on His earth .. So the prayer of the wronged on earth is a knock on the King's door and a complaint to Him. Would the King see an injustice and then it be as if the injustice never happened? Far be that from Allah the Almighty, the King, our Lord. But as I said months ago about my experience with one of the aggressive YouTubers, who transgressed by slandering honor and left no evil word unsaid, in front of everyone, for 3 years: one day one of the brothers asked me about the answering of prayer against the wrongdoer. I wrote that day that while the wrongdoer mocks Allah's threat, the wronged must not despair of Allah's help! Both are being tested. The wrongdoer is tested and the wronged is tested. The wrongdoer is tested: will he turn back, or will his self's craving and its whim grow fiercer in him? For a wrongdoer may be given years of time to turn back and he does not. As for the wronged, he deposits the file of his case with the King and does not keep saying every hour: "When .. when .." For he is being tested in his anger over the wrong done to him: will he transgress .. will he retaliate .. will he take his right by his hand or his tongue after depositing the file of his case with the King? Or will he be patient, awaiting the King's judgment? So, as we see, the test is not only for the wrongdoer. Whoever is wronged, does not take his right by hand or tongue and deposits his case with his Lord must await the judgment without his soul being agitated and saying "The punishment is late .. the punishment is late .." That is not your business as the wronged. Yes, the punishment is delayed, because the wrongdoer, for example, has a daughter he must provide for for a period of time before the punishment descends on him! Because the wrongdoer, for example, has a family, a family that did no wrong and needs him to establish for it a house or a farm to shelter in at its time of need, so he has to prepare for his family what it needs before the punishment befalls him! The world was not created for your sake, O wronged one, so that you say: "I was wronged, I want my right now!" No, the world was not created only for your needs. The world is complicated .. it has very complicated details .. it has entanglements hidden from no one and known to all .. The world is individual and collective destinies .. The wrongdoer does wrong, but this wrongdoer has a soul that has not yet completed its provision, and a family who have not yet completed what they are meant to get from this wrongdoer, and perhaps he will wrong others but has not wronged them yet. So when your right comes to you early, you are asking for the worldly order to be disrupted for your sake! That is a strange thing! The world was not created only for the wronged, so that the moment he is wronged his right is taken for him. It is natural for anger to remain in your chest. The wrongdoer's punishment may be postponed a year, two or three while your chest is full of anger. Imagine a person who wakes in the morning to a creature slandering his honor before millions of people .. telling him before millions of people: "You trade in your wives" .. Muslim women .. veiled .. who stand the night in prayer .. merely because he disagreed with that person .. And the waiting for the punishment to descend on him goes on, but it is the waiting of the forbearing, confident, unhurried one who is not preoccupied with "when"! Who has no "when" in his daily life! Yet as a wronged person, whatever the kind of wrong done to you, do not blame yourself for being angry. That is natural.
The experiences of injustice people have suffered are many; injustice occurs daily, around the clock, without pause. I do not know the size of injustice among people today; only our Lord the King knows. But it is frightening in size, quantity and kind, terrifying and shattering, and whoever does not see it on earth is blind in sight and insight.""")

t(38, 2235, """People in this world are holders of rights before they are bearers of duties. One single smile on the face of one single small child means there is a whole system working in secret to make this child safe, at ease and happy, living a normal life and receiving his rights as a child! And to make the grandfather safe! And to make the grandmother safe! And to keep the man and his wife in safety! A system that sees what society does not see! That grasps what society does not grasp! That works behind the scenes! The unknown soldiers on whose shoulders states are built, societies become stable, justice prevails and all people without exception are made happy! It is a system that does not rejoice as people rejoice, because it does not have the time that people have! It is a system that does not find the time to live people's life! It does not find the way to be safe from every kind of treachery, harm and targeting as people are safe .. It is the system that is always targeted .. because eliminating its members means shaking the system and perhaps crushing it .. A salute to every unknown soldier in this world who was and still is a lofty soul, glad that it serves people and makes them happy, even if the body and self of him / her did not enjoy the same life and comfort as others! To these monotheist men and women, peace from us .. And peace be upon them, men and women, on the Day when people stand before the Lord of the worlds!""")

t(40, 805, """The real beginning of the fall of the Roman Empire was an economic beginning, not a military one (not a military defeat before another nation), but an internal economic collapse. Because of the enormous pressure that raising the army's salaries put on the state budget and its stock of gold (the maker of stability), the state was forced to make currency from ((copper)), which has no value in people's eyes .. People lost confidence in their country's currency .. Prices inflated madly, daily, because people said: what is in our hands is cheap copper .. a mere metal of no value .. And merchants did not feel safe owning copper .. Copper in coins is like wood or iron, worthless .. Gold, and only gold, through the different ages of man, and with it real silver to a lesser degree, were the two elements of economic and financial security for any nation. On the basis of a nation's possession of gold its economy could withstand local or regional fluctuations .. Since 1944 the world decided to use copper .. (paper currencies) in a final, definitive, permanent, continuous and settled way .. Today's economy is the economy of copper .. and rescue will be only in gold .. the metal that guarantees the cycle of financial and economic life .. You build me a steamship costing a billion and take paper of no value, which you cannot convince people of if that paper currency's value suffers a crisis; or you take gold from me, which, when you go bankrupt, you use within your society, and everyone wants it because it is gold and everyone is convinced it is a constant element of security?

Everyone wants gold, in every country and every nation throughout history .. Man will go on being convinced by nothing above gold; man has nothing more than gold that can make him feel financial security .. Any nation that sells its crops and produce and obtains gold: this means the cycle of exchange inside that nation turns on a currency that has value .. The Chinese farmer, when he is paid the price of his crop in gold, can speak to his Chinese society as one who owns real money .. A Western factory owner who makes something and is paid gold for it can rest assured that he owns real money.

Gold is not merely a currency that the seller of a farm crop, or the one who makes goods, tools and devices, receives and then rejoices and says: "I have gold!" That is not what the matter is at root! The reason for the joy of owning gold is that gold is considered the highest element of security among all humans in guaranteeing wealth, the stability of its value and its continuing to have actual value. A safe in a crop seller's house with real gold in it, and a safe in a car-factory owner's house with real gold in it, are not like a safe holding banknotes that lose their value and are manipulated by dozens of local and foreign parties.

Gold in the merchant's safe, whether he is a farmer or an industrialist, means he owns real money .. As simple as that .. People, simply, throughout history and until — Allah knows best — the end of the world, will keep trusting gold and considering it something precious .. But the important thing, the condition, is that gold not spread in the hands of ((all the nations of the world)) as if it were water, so that it loses its value and comes within everyone's reach (except within the reach of one nation, by the text of a hadith with a sound chain). Then there will be one nation (only) whose sons possess much gold, and around them, east and west, poor nations in need of this nation's gold, taking from it on fair terms through trade .. The nation that will be provided with limitless gold will barter with the other nations for food, luxurious houses, furniture, devices, cars and everything, and individuals in the other nations that do not own gold will start saying: Come, let us farm to sell to the nation of gold .. Come, let us manufacture to sell to the nation of gold .. This will ease the pressure on the governments of East and West, provide job opportunities for their peoples, run their factories, help them in agricultural production, guarantee political stability for their governments and prevent unrest in their countries. The nation that will possess the gold will be a refuge and a blessing for the nations of the earth.

So what is coming in the history of the world is full power and full dominance over the world through the wealth of gold .. Whoever possesses more gold will rule the world, because currencies will not hold out with the fall of the world order, and humanity will need to recycle the economy, remake money and redefine the foundations of successful financial thought. So there will be a global grinding over the mountain of the Euphrates before they lose it and it goes to those who deserve it, only those who deserve it.""")

t(41, 1000, """I have not found a (godly) scholar, well-grounded in the science of hadith, among the hadith scholars, to whom a contradiction between a hadith and a verse in the Book of Allah Most High was brought, without his ruling the hadith weak in chain / text, or that the narrator was confused, or that the narrator forgot and did not hear well. As the Lady Aisha, Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her, once said: "Abu Hurayra misheard", when she was asked about the contradiction in the hadith that the child of adultery is the worst of the three, and the hadith's plain conflict with the Book of Allah Most High. The hadith was specific to a certain, particular child who had harmed the Prophet ﷺ, so it was a ruling specific to a particular child; perhaps revelation informed the Prophet ﷺ that there was evil in this child's conduct .. This scrutiny and examination of hadiths is what protects the Ummah from falling into disasters. The disasters are many; disastrous foundations were laid for them in people's lives, and juristic understandings were built on them, at times mistaken and at other times corrupt in argument. Thus the Ummah was lost for long centuries after the death of the first generation of the noble Companions, to whom one returns for decisive statements. After them came the mujtahids, and they were right and wrong .. then wrong and right, and right and wrong .. In any case .. it is established for people more and more every day, by following the scholars specialized in the science of hadith in particular, that everything that contradicts the explicit Qur'an is not authentic from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So do not take the meaning of any hadith that opposes the explicit Qur'an from the mouth of non-specialists; they, as hadith scholars, are more able, by the power of Allah Most High, to prove to you the weakness of every hadith that opposes the explicit Book of Allah Most High, the Almighty, our Lord.""")

t(41, 1700, """Honoring children comes through spouses treating each other well .. In the calm home, the children are honored .. So fear Allah, servants of Allah, men and women, regarding offspring .. Except one who has been wronged, woman or man .. May Allah make for him .. or make for her .. a way, relief and victory, and be compassionate and gentle with the children wherever they are""")

t(42, 340, """Girls (they), yes, especially in this time of ours, because they are weak .. May Allah our Lord help fathers and mothers .. O young husbands .. O mothers-in-law .. fear Allah .. fear Allah regarding people's daughters .. And know that the punishment of injustice is great on a Day when regret will not avail. How many a husband has entered the Fire over a wife! And how many a husband's mother has entered the Fire over a son's wife! Fear Allah for your flesh on the Day of Resurrection .. for your skins .. Let no person come on the Day of Resurrection saying: "I did not know, I had no idea that this is what would happen to me" .. On that Day the screaming will be loud .. the pains and aches successive, never stopping .. the moaning and wailing in Hell prolonged, unbroken .. And the poor wronged woman will be strutting in bliss .. a crowned, pampered queen .. while the husband and his mother are wretched in the Fire together; the son and his mother keep each other company in the fire of Hell, insulting each other and cursing each other .. The son and his mother .. Indeed they hit each other .. and spit on each other .. The son and his mother .. That is true and will be .. The girl they wronged looks at them and says: Praise be to Allah who took my right for me .. Rot in the Fire more and more .. This is the station you both deserve .. So let whoever has grown comfortable with injustice fear Allah, to save his skin, his flesh and his dignity!""")

t(42, 1830, """A bridge, then relief for us all, Allah Most High willing .. And women, across the lands of their Ummah, will have an abundant share of life, by the power of Allah Most High""")

t(43, 490, """The hall for collecting Bayt al-Maqdis passports, by the power of our Lord""")

t(43, 1560, """An artificial-intelligence image, not of a real child .. A weaned child crying .. In human relationships there is a weaning that people practice toward each other .. A very large number of people practice weaning toward each other .. Then, when the axe falls on the head, they are amazed that people draw away from them .. The husband drawing away from his wife .. The wife drawing away from her husband .. Siblings drawing away from each other .. Friends drawing away from each other .. The reason is very clear, but it is hidden from them; they do not see it .. They discover the size of the mistake they committed only when they reap the results, and the results are very disastrous .. The results are one person being weaned off another .. Unfortunately, those who practice the behavior of weaning as a punishment for a wife .. or a punishment for a husband .. or a punishment for any person in their social surroundings do not know that weaning, time after time after time, ends in psychological weaning, which is a thousand times more dangerous than the other kinds of weaning .. Psychological weaning is very dangerous and its results are disastrous, because they strike the depth of a person's sense of his dignity in a vital spot .. The one who practices the method of weaning on you time after time strikes you in your dignity, so you get angry for it and avenge it by his leaving your heart and turning into something ordinary .. He is present, fine .. he is absent, fine! Here people begin to reap the results of their wrong conduct, but it is a bitter harvest.""")

t(44, 560, """Dear brothers .. commenting on one of today's comments .. There is no such thing as the art of Islamic architecture from a religious standpoint .. Using the term "Islamic architecture" as if it were a matter related to religion and legislation is a big mistake .. because this would mean that Muslims over 1447 years built their houses and everything in their cities according to Qur'anic texts telling them: build such-and-such wall like this, the roof must be like this and the door must be like this. That of course is not true; the way of building has no connection with any verse in the Book of our Almighty Lord, hallowed be His names, or with the sayings of the Prophet ﷺ. If the architecture of Muslims, as a model, method and architectural style, is described as "Islamic architecture", that is only because those who founded this art were Muslims, no more and no less. It would have been more correct not to attach the word Islamic to the art of architecture, because this would cause confusion in the understanding of many people, as has in fact happened! Muslims have an architectural art through history and up to today: in India and Pakistan it is other than Turkey's, in Turkey other than Egypt's and North Africa's, in the Arabian Peninsula other than all of them, in Yemen other than all the aforementioned, and in Azerbaijan, Turkmenistan and other Islamic Central Asian countries there are different patterns, forms and details! And from before that there still stand examples such as the Umayyad, Abbasid, Andalusian, Fatimid and Mamluk monuments! So where is the Islamic art of architecture? It is more correct to understand that the art of architecture is a purely human effort and purely human ijtihad. So you, as a Muslim, should not, if your Muslim neighbor builds a building in the Belgian style, say of him that he has gone against Islam and gone against the Sharia! That is wrong talk .. Nor should you, if you enter a Muslim city whose architecture is derived from European art that has no crosses, no statues, no trait of disbelief and no hint of disbelief from near or far, but is only a Western architectural model, say: "I seek Allah's forgiveness, what is this?!" This comes from not understanding realities correctly, and from minds being closed to grasping things correctly. The art of (Islamic) architecture — an inaccurate phrase, but one people have grown used to — is human ijtihad .. the ijtihad of humans .. humans who liked the idea of making a roof shaped like this .. and a wall shaped like this .. not to mention the environmental factors, which have a wide and great influence on building patterns among all humans. The European, the Turk and others, in all the lands of snow, when they made sloping roofs, did they make them sloping because the Torah and the Gospel contain texts on how the roof's shape is to be built? The subject has nothing to do with religion; rather, rain made that inevitable for all the people of rainy lands where heavy snow falls, even in the farthest east of Asia and in North America across thousands of years, where the tents of the native inhabitants came out sloping, and even the houses of the Eskimo are sloping, where there was neither Torah nor Gospel! And Allah is the One whose help is sought.""")

t(44, 2500, """In a post this morning I spoke about the will of the people of the Fire and set out my view on it in detail. One of the dear brothers then raised a question about that will: whether it is a will in which the side of means is granted to the people of the Fire, because of the verse the dear brother mentioned in his question, which is the very verse on whose meaning the reply here was built. Whereas I had said in my explanation about""")

t(45, 150, """the will of the people of the Fire that it is a will without means, because means are cut off from them in the Fire entirely and forbidden to them, and it is merely a will of wishing and desire, no more; contrary to the view of the dear questioning brother, who held that the mere fact that they are returned after the attempt to flee means that means are available to them to carry out their will, in success or failure. So I answered the dear brother at length to clear up the matter for him. Before copying my reply here for the general benefit, it is important that we recall the saying of our Almighty Lord, hallowed be His names, magnified in the heavens and on earth and exalted in great loftiness, about the state the dear questioning brother asked about: the attempt of the people of the Fire to get out of it, and his considering that this means their will was followed by means they undertook; because the attempt to flee is a taking of means, from his point of view, which he put forward as discussion, not dispute, may Allah honor him. Whereas in truth, if we examine the matter, we will know that means are forbidden to them. We see in the Book of our Lord the saying of our Almighty Lord, hallowed be His names: {"Whenever they want to get out of it, out of anguish, they are returned into it, and: Taste the punishment of the burning"} .. We see the saying of our Almighty Lord "returned into it", and not "returned to it"! This noble verse had slipped my mind when I explained to the brother in my reply to his question this morning; then I remembered the verse and said: Glory be to our Almighty Lord. Our Almighty Lord says "returned into it" and not "returned to it". This is a clear indication that means are not available at all for them to take, which is what I showed in the post where I spoke of the will of the people of the Fire. Had means been available for them to get out of it, some would have succeeded and some failed, and the wording of the verse could not have been "returned into it"; there would then have been a rational and logical clash on reading the verse. Had means been available to the people of the Fire, some succeeding in fleeing and some failing, the verse would have had to be: "returned to it" .. with "returned to it" meaning those who succeeded in fleeing and used means that enabled them to flee. But Allah Most High, our Almighty Lord, said "returned into it", and this means that they try to flee while they are in it and never reach its outside. This means the fall of all means there, and that means there are not created for them and not granted to them at all. Had there been means created for them there, some of them would have succeeded in fleeing to outside it and been brought back to it, and the noble verse would have been "returned to it", not "returned into it".

And this was my reply to the dear questioning brother's question, for whoever wants more: And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Perhaps there is a wall in it that they head toward, and outside the wall is not fire! Here they are not taking means, because the wall is in the same place. A movement inside the perimeter of the crisis is not counted as taking means. Taking means is that you go outside the crisis to activate the tools; that is, you put at least one foot outside the crisis, so that the means move you, even by 1%, outside the crisis. If taking means were to be written for them in the Fire, they would have to scale the wall and get out of the Fire entirely and then be returned. Then yes, they would have taken means and left the crisis entirely; or partially, by reaching the wall and being between the Fire and what is beyond it without leaving it entirely; then yes, their taking of means would occur. But what if the wall is curved, not vertical, and they try to climb it from below, hoping to rise to its top, and they slide down the wall because it is curved, while they are inside the Fire? This is an attempt of a will to get out, as the verse mentions, an attempt expressing a wish .. a wish to get out .. a will whose title is wish only, with no taking of real or considerable means in it, because means are not permitted to exist in the Fire at all. So the saying of our Almighty Lord, (Whenever they want to get out of it), is not the wording of a will followed by real means, but a will of wishing. You want to become a pilot, you want; all you do, for example, is browse information on how to become a pilot, only .. You do nothing else. Here you have not activated the tools of means ..""")

t(45, 1730, """As has come in the report: And to the people return their harmony and their blessing, the near of them and the far of them.""")

t(46, 355, """Our brother in the picture says: (The second universality of Islam begins only with conditions, among them that people commit adultery in the streets, on the pavements, completely naked; and this, to him, is the condition for the earth's being filled with injustice and oppression to be realized). To our brother it is one of the conditions for the earth's being filled with injustice and oppression to be realized. The cause of this is what we all warned against throughout our gathering here. We all said, with one understanding: First, those who studied Sharia knowledge are not prophets who do not err, while people (most of them) follow the way of sanctifying and ascribing infallibility to everyone who wears a turban and grows a beard!

Second, I had written here months ago: Most of the Shia sanctified the Household of the Prophet and asserted their infallibility, and most of the Sunnis sanctified their sheikhs and asserted their infallibility, except those of the people of the Sunnah whom Allah Most High guided and protected; so both parties are equal in misguidance! Hence (((many of))) the people, not all the people, are still like blind followers in religious thought: once a man puts on a turban or a cap and speaks about religion, they say "You are right". The reason is the absence of knowledge from people, so they believe on opinion, not on evidence. The man came out and spoke by opinion, and some people think opinion is evidence and text. That too is only from their ignorance; they do not know the meaning of the word (evidence), and they think that what the Prophet ﷺ said is explained by a barren opinion. They do not know that the knowledge of the end of time is something big and great, not to be handled the way the brother in the picture handled it, with this intellectual vulgarity, most regrettably.

Most regrettably, the view becomes clear to us all after a long journey of watching and observing, and it is a view whose concealment is a betrayal of Allah, His Messenger and the believers. The truth that must never be concealed among people is: Specializing in Sharia knowledge is not proof of the acumen of the person who specialized in Sharia knowledge. Specializing in Sharia knowledge is not proof of the sound mind of the person who specialized in Sharia knowledge, his wisdom or his ability to see things correctly. Specializing in Sharia knowledge is not proof that the person's mind is an analytical, alert, keen mind able to see everything clearly. Specializing in Sharia knowledge is not proof that the one who specialized is smarter than you, or that he is more able than you to understand the religion, if you are mindful of Allah, revere Him and fear Him and He opens for you a door of understanding He did not open for the one who specialized in Sharia knowledge, even if he spent his whole life studying Sharia knowledge. Mindfulness of Allah Most High and fear of Him are a thousand times more important than studying Sharia knowledge at a university, while how many of those who studied Sharia knowledge at universities did not apply what they learned of the Book of their Lord and the hadiths of their Prophet ﷺ. Sharia knowledge is a crown for whoever learns it, acts on it and is mindful of Allah, so that Allah Most High opens to him the openings of the knowers, on top of knowledge and memorization. That is a thing of utmost beauty.""")

t(46, 2400, """Continuing what was discussed yesterday about the mashi'a (will) of the people of Paradise .. today we speak (meaning we all gather), we speak about the irada (will) of the people of the Fire, seeking refuge in Allah Most High from it for us, for all our offspring and for all our loved ones

What is noticeable is that what has come regarding the people of the Fire, while they are in the Fire, is that they have (irada), not mashi'a; irada came regarding them as in saying "they wanted .. they want .." Whoever read the two posts I published here in writing yesterday will remember that the people of Paradise were given (mashi'a). We said that irada is the attribute and mark of worldly life; we, in the abode of this world, have irada. We said that man's irada is not like the irada of Allah Most High, and we said that the irada of the Lord, hallowed be His names, is an effective mashi'a; as for""")

t(47, 150, """man's irada in the abode of this world, it does not guarantee that a thing comes about, and we said this is among the attributes of living in the deficient abode of this world. And we said (meaning we talked together and discussed; the "we" here does not refer to me the writer, refuge is sought in Allah Most High), we said that man's irada may be fulfilled by Allah Most High or not fulfilled in the abode of this world, whereas in Paradise it turns into an irada fulfilled in everything; that is why it moved from the name irada to the name mashi'a. What appears, then, to one who ponders the Book of Allah Most High is that the people of the Fire move to the Fire and take with them the attribute of irada from this world, and they have no mashi'a, as the verses in the Book of our Almighty Lord indicate, in that in the Fire they (want). But since the irada of the accountable one being tested in the abode of this world may be carried out or prevented, the irada of the people of the Fire in the Fire is the opposite of their state when they were in the abode of this world: their irada in the Fire is always prevented. When one of them in the abode of this world wanted a thing, it would happen for him or not happen, just like the believer; but his irada, that is, of the one of the people of the Fire while in the Fire, differs from his irada in this world, in that his irada in the Fire is rejected always, not sometimes. If they want water they are given scalding water; if they want food they are given zaqqum; and if they want to get out of it they are returned into it. Of all their irada not a single irada is fulfilled.

This is a clarification of the meaning of irada passing with them from the abode of this world to the abode of the Hereafter. It is irada in the sense of wishing a thing would happen; there is no door of striving in it, as is the case with worldly irada, but mere wishing with the fall of all means. In the Fire, if they wanted cold water, there is no room there for taking means so that the irada comes to be fulfilled! Whereas in this world they were possessors of an irada subject to means, if Allah willed their success; but in the Fire Allah withholds from them His granting of success. One of them, a disbeliever in this world, would want a thing and strive for it by means, and Allah Most High would grant him success in achieving what he wanted. But in the Fire, if he wanted a thousand wants in a single moment, not one want of them would be fulfilled. This, then, is the reality of the irada of the people of the Fire while they are in the Fire.""")

t(47, 1145, """It has come in the report: The Muslims will sleep after the Isha prayer and will wake for Fajr, but it will be pitch dark when they wake for the prayer .. So one of them will say to himself: "Perhaps I slept only a little, so let me finish my sleep!" Then they will wake, each in his house and home, hours later, to pray Fajr, and will again find the darkness pitch black and intense. One of them will say to himself: "Perhaps I slept only a little, so let me sleep a little and then wake." Then when one of them wakes, he looks at the sky and finds the darkness pitch black and intense again. The report, which I read 25 years ago, most likely in al-Fitan by Nu'aym ibn Hammad, continues: They remain like that for days — I think it is 3 days — until they go out to one another's houses, as the report says, asking one another in astonishment. When the three days have passed, the sun comes out from its west.

In this report there is a very important benefit besides the benefit of explaining what precedes the rising of the sun from its west, which is something children and grandchildren should memorize; perhaps they will be among the people of that hard moment. The second benefit is that this report mentions that the Muslims at the time of the sun's rising from its west (do not pray Fajr in intense pitch darkness, as happens today in many mosques)! This is because the second universality of Islam will correct the time of Fajr for all Muslims and make them all pray at the time of the true dawn. The report confirms this conclusion! So although the report is classified as weak, it mentions something a hadith narrator could not make up: how would someone composing a text know that many Muslims before the second universality of Islam would pray Fajr at the time of intense pitch darkness?!

Note: Not all mosques of the Islamic world pray at the wrong time; many mosques of the Islamic world pray at the time of the true dawn.""")
